<span id="S1.T1.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:150.0pt;">
<span id="S1.T1.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximum possible <math id="S1.T1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> grows with at least <math id="S1.T1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-1)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-1)!</annotation></semantics></math>; <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 3.10. ‣ 3.3 Complete Graphs ‣ 3 Period Lengths of Parallel Chip-Firing Games ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Complete bipartite <math id="S1.T1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{a,\,b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{a,\,b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:100.0pt;">
<span id="S1.T1.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.T1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=i</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S1.T1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S1.T1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq\min(a,\,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq\min(a,\,b)</annotation></semantics></math>; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang (2010)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S1.T1.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="S1.T1.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:150.0pt;">
<span id="S1.T1.2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximum possible <math id="S1.T1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> grows with at least <math id="S1.T1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(a,\,b)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(a,\,b)!</annotation></semantics></math>; <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem15" title="Theorem 3.15. ‣ 3.4 Complete Bipartite Graphs ‣ 3 Period Lengths of Parallel Chip-Firing Games ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.15</span></a></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>The period lengths <math id="S1.T1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> of parallel chip-firing games on special classes of graphs.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define a <em id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">directed graph</em> <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(V,\,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(V,\,E)</annotation></semantics></math> as a set of vertices <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and a set of ordered pairs of vertices (<em id="S2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">edges</em>) <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. The edge <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\,v)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,\,v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,\,v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be <em id="S2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">directed from <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math></em>. We define an <em id="S2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">orientation</em> of an undirected graph <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,\,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,\,E)</annotation></semantics></math> to be a directed graph <math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(V,\,E^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(V,\,E^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> such that either <math id="S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\,v)\in E^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\,v)\in E^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v,\,u)\in E^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v,\,u)\in E^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if there exists an edge between <math id="S2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, but there do not exist vertices <math id="S2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\,v)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v,\,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v,\,u)</annotation></semantics></math> are both elements in <math id="S2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">in-degree</em> of a vertex <math id="S2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted <math id="S2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg^{-}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>deg</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg^{-}v</annotation></semantics></math> and is the number of edges directed from another vertex to <math id="S2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">out-degree</em> of a vertex <math id="S2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted <math id="S2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg^{+}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>deg</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg^{+}v</annotation></semantics></math> and is the number of edges directed from <math id="S2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to another vertex. In the directed graph in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg^{+}v_{3}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>deg</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg^{+}v_{3}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg^{-}v_{3}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>deg</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg^{-}v_{3}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">degree</em> of a vertex <math id="S2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted <math id="S2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg v</annotation></semantics></math> and is the total number of edges including <math id="S2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. In Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg v_{3}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg v_{3}=3</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">distance</em> between two vertices <math id="S2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the length of the shortest path from <math id="S2.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and is denoted <math id="S2.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(u,\,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(u,\,v)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the undirected graph in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S2.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v_{1},\,v_{4})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v_{1},\,v_{4})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. In the directed graph, <math id="S2.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v_{1},\,v_{4})=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v_{1},\,v_{4})=3</annotation></semantics></math>. For parallel chip-firing games on directed graphs, a vertex fires when the number of chips it possesses exceeds its out-degree, upon which the vertex fires one chip across each outgoing edge.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="83.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 142.84 83.78" width="142.84"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="translate(0,83.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(12.36,0) translate(0,71.42)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 11.81 0 C 11.81 6.52 6.52 11.81 0 11.81 C -6.52 11.81 -11.81 6.52 -11.81 0 C -11.81 -6.52 -6.52 -11.81 0 -11.81 C 6.52 -11.81 11.81 -6.52 11.81 0 Z M 0 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.94 -3.57)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 90.55 0 C 90.55 6.52 85.26 11.81 78.74 11.81 C 72.22 11.81 66.93 6.52 66.93 0 C 66.93 -6.52 72.22 -11.81 78.74 -11.81 C 85.26 -11.81 90.55 -6.52 90.55 0 Z M 78.74 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 75.8 -3.57)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 51.18 -59.06 C 51.18 -52.53 45.89 -47.24 39.37 -47.24 C 32.85 -47.24 27.56 -52.53 27.56 -59.06 C 27.56 -65.58 32.85 -70.87 39.37 -70.87 C 45.89 -70.87 51.18 -65.58 51.18 -59.06 Z M 39.37 -59.06"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 36.43 -62.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 129.92 -59.06 C 129.92 -52.53 124.63 -47.24 118.11 -47.24 C 111.59 -47.24 106.3 -52.53 106.3 -59.06 C 106.3 -65.58 111.59 -70.87 118.11 -70.87 C 124.63 -70.87 129.92 -65.58 129.92 -59.06 Z M 118.11 -59.06"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 115.17 -62.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 12.36 0 L 66.38 0"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 71.88 -10.29 L 46.23 -48.77"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 51.73 -59.06 L 105.75 -59.06"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 6.86 -10.29 L 32.51 -48.77"></path></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="83.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 142.84 83.78" width="142.84"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,83.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(12.36,0) translate(0,71.42)"><g stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 11.81 0 C 11.81 6.52 6.52 11.81 0 11.81 C -6.52 11.81 -11.81 6.52 -11.81 0 C -11.81 -6.52 -6.52 -11.81 0 -11.81 C 6.52 -11.81 11.81 -6.52 11.81 0 Z M 0 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.94 -3.57)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 90.55 0 C 90.55 6.52 85.26 11.81 78.74 11.81 C 72.22 11.81 66.93 6.52 66.93 0 C 66.93 -6.52 72.22 -11.81 78.74 -11.81 C 85.26 -11.81 90.55 -6.52 90.55 0 Z M 78.74 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 75.8 -3.57)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 51.18 -59.06 C 51.18 -52.53 45.89 -47.24 39.37 -47.24 C 32.85 -47.24 27.56 -52.53 27.56 -59.06 C 27.56 -65.58 32.85 -70.87 39.37 -70.87 C 45.89 -70.87 51.18 -65.58 51.18 -59.06 Z M 39.37 -59.06"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 36.43 -62.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 129.92 -59.06 C 129.92 -52.53 124.63 -47.24 118.11 -47.24 C 111.59 -47.24 106.3 -52.53 106.3 -59.06 C 106.3 -65.58 111.59 -70.87 118.11 -70.87 C 124.63 -70.87 129.92 -65.58 129.92 -59.06 Z M 118.11 -59.06"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 115.17 -62.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 12.36 0 L 65.39 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.64pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 65.39 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.16 2.88 C -1.98 1.8 0 0.18 0.54 0 C 0 -0.18 -1.98 -1.8 -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 71.88 -10.29 L 46.77 -47.95"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.64pt" transform="matrix(-0.5547 -0.83205 0.83205 -0.5547 46.77 -47.95)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.16 2.88 C -1.98 1.8 0 0.18 0.54 0 C 0 -0.18 -1.98 -1.8 -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 32.51 -48.77 L 7.4 -11.11"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.64pt" transform="matrix(-0.5547 0.83205 -0.83205 -0.5547 7.4 -11.11)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.16 2.88 C -1.98 1.8 0 0.18 0.54 0 C 0 -0.18 -1.98 -1.8 -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 51.73 -59.06 L 104.76 -59.06"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.64pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 104.76 -59.06)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.16 2.88 C -1.98 1.8 0 0.18 0.54 0 C 0 -0.18 -1.98 -1.8 -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>An undirected graph <math id="S2.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> (left) and an orientation of <math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Bitar and Goles <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bitar and Goles (1992)</a></cite> noted that the fixed numbers of chips and vertices make every parallel chip-firing game on a finite undirected graph periodic. Prisner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Prisner (1994)</a></cite> noted that the same is true for parallel chip-firing games on finite directed graphs. We say that a parallel chip-firing game on a directed graph has period <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest integer for which there exists a round <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that every vertex has the same number of chips in round <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as in round <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+T</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the least such <math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as round 0. Let <math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of chips on a vertex <math id="S2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> at the beginning of round <math id="S2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="S2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> fires on round <math id="S2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> if it does not. Let <math id="S2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v}=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}F_{t}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v}=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}F_{t}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be the total number of times <math id="S2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> fires in the first <math id="S2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> rounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We say that a directed graph <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(V,\,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(V,\,E)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strongly connected</em> if there exists a path in both directions between every pair of vertices <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v,\,u\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v,\,u\in V</annotation></semantics></math>. A <em id="S2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strongly connected component</em> of <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is a subgraph of <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> that is strongly connected and maximal: no more vertices or edges may be included while keeping the subgraph strongly connected. We let the <em id="S2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">condensation</em> of a directed graph <math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be a directed graph with all strongly connected components of <math id="S2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> as vertices. Borrowing notation from Prisner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Prisner (1994)</a></cite>, we define a <em id="S2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sink component</em> as a strongly connected component that forms a sink in the condensation of <math id="S2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. In Figure <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, SCC3 is a sink component. We say that a vertex is <em id="S2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">forever passive</em> if it does not fire in all future states.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="S2.F2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.F2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:347.4pt;position:relative; bottom:-28.5pt;">
<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="165.24" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 471.51 165.24" width="471.51"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,165.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(256.46,0) translate(0,85.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -224.41 39.37 C -224.41 45.89 -229.7 51.18 -236.22 51.18 C -242.74 51.18 -248.03 45.89 -248.03 39.37 C -248.03 32.85 -242.74 27.56 -236.22 27.56 C -229.7 27.56 -224.41 32.85 -224.41 39.37 Z M -236.22 39.37"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -241.41 34.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text">A</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -185.04 39.37 C -185.04 45.89 -190.33 51.18 -196.85 51.18 C -203.37 51.18 -208.66 45.89 -208.66 39.37 C -208.66 32.85 -203.37 27.56 -196.85 27.56 C -190.33 27.56 -185.04 32.85 -185.04 39.37 Z M -196.85 39.37"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -201.75 34.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F2.pic1.2" class="ltx_text">B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -185.04 0 C -185.04 6.52 -190.33 11.81 -196.85 11.81 C -203.37 11.81 -208.66 6.52 -208.66 0 C -208.66 -6.52 -203.37 -1