<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>An example of a parallel chip-firing game from <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. Here <math id="S4.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=11000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=11000</annotation></semantics></math> is not periodic, and <math id="S4.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S4.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as its atomic firing sequence.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> fails to construct a parallel chip-firing game in which a vertex has <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as its atomic firing sequence if <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is periodic with period <math id="S4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case the construction yields a parallel chip-firing game with <math id="S4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=k&lt;\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=k&lt;\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. To show that a periodic binary string can be the atomic firing sequence of a vertex, we turn to our main theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(s)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the length of a binary string <math id="S4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(s)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of 1s in <math id="S4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, let <math id="S4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(s)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k(s)\leq\ell(s)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k(s)\leq\ell(s)-1</annotation></semantics></math> be the maximum value such that <math id="S4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k(s)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k(s)}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(s)=\ell(s)-1-k(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(s)=\ell(s)-1-k(s)</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of trailing zeros in <math id="S4.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1010" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1010</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1010</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(s)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(s)=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(s)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(s)=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(s)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=111000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>111000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=111000</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(s)=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(s)=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(s)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(s)=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(s)=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(s)=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">In the following proof, we augment the construction from <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> to construct a parallel chip-firing game on a directed graph in which a vertex has a periodic atomic firing sequence. To do so, we draw inspiration from Jiang, Scully, and Zhang’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al. (2015)</a></cite> proof of Theorem 4.1 and construct a parallel chip-firing game by attaching many copies of a graph to a single vertex.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any binary string <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> that contains 1, there exists a parallel chip-firing game on a directed graph such that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is the firing sequence of some vertex <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For brevity, we let <math id="S4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=\ell(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=\ell(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. We also let <math id="S4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=k(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=k(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we refer to <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">We create <math id="S4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n</annotation></semantics></math> copies of the simple cycle <math id="S4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and label them <math id="S4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0},\,C^{1},\,\ldots,\,C^{2n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0},\,C^{1},\,\ldots,\,C^{2n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the <math id="S4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th vertex in <math id="S4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. We assign an initial configuration of chips in each cycle in the same way as in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>: <math id="S4.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(v_{i}^{j})=s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(v_{i}^{j})=s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, we replace all the <math id="S4.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> with a single vertex <math id="S4.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, there exist edges directed from <math id="S4.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and from <math id="S4.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\ell-1}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\ell-1}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="S4.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has 0 chips if <math id="S4.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S4.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n</annotation></semantics></math> chips if <math id="S4.p14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(v_{i}^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(v_{i}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="S4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}(v_{i}^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}(v_{i}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="S4.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, collecting all the <math id="S4.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> into one vertex does not change <math id="S4.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}(v_{i}^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}(v_{i}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, <math id="S4.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S4.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as its length-<math id="S4.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> firing sequence. We now augment the graph to force <math id="S4.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="S4.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, regardless of whether <math id="S4.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is periodic.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">We add a new vertex, <math id="S4.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, with an edge directed from <math id="S4.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. We also add <math id="S4.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> directed paths of <math id="S4.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> vertices each. We will call these paths <em id="S4.p16.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">waterfalls</em>. If <math id="S4.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead add <math id="S4.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> single vertices (as if <math id="S4.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>). We label the <math id="S4.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th vertex in the <math id="S4.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th waterfall <math id="S4.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math>. We add edges directed from <math id="S4.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and from <math id="S4.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{d-1}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{d-1}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="S4.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(u)=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(u)=n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(u_{0}^{j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(u_{0}^{j})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead set <math id="S4.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(u_{d-1}^{j})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(u_{d-1}^{j})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(u)=c_{0}(u_{i}^{j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(u)=c_{0}(u_{i}^{j})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq d-2</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S4.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. In both cases, we also place <math id="S4.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> more chips onto <math id="S4.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="S4.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(v)=s_{0}(2n)+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(v)=s_{0}(2n)+n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, on the first round of the game, each vertex <math id="S4.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{d-1}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{d-1}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> fires its 1 chip to <math id="S4.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. This will give <math id="S4.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> a total of <math id="S4.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n</annotation></semantics></math> chips, ignoring the behavior of the cycles. Since <math id="S4.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg^{+}v=2n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>deg</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg^{+}v=2n+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="S4.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> will only have enough chips to fire when <math id="S4.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so it will still have <math id="S4.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as its length-<math id="S4.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> firing sequence. On round <math id="S4.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\ell-d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\ell-d-1</annotation></semantics></math>, vertex <math id="S4.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> will fire for the <math id="S4.p18.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>th time, so that <math id="S4.p18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k+1}(u)=n=\deg^{+}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>deg</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k+1}(u)=n=\deg^{+}u</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.p18.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> will fire one chip to each <math id="S4.p18.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> on round <math id="S4.p18.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Over the next <math id="S4.p18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-1</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, these <math id="S4.p18.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> chips will flow down the waterfalls. Then on round <math id="S4.p18.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we will have <math id="S4.p18.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}(u_{i}^{j})=c_{0}(u_{i}^{j})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}(u_{i}^{j})=c_{0}(u_{i}^{j})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We also have <math id="S4.p18.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}(v_{i}^{j})=c_{0}(v_{i}^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}(v_{i}^{j})=c_{0}(v_{i}^{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p18.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}(v)=c_{0}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}(v)=c_{0}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> by the cyclic construction of the <math id="S4.p18.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, <math id="S4.p18.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}(u)=c_{0}(u)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}(u)=c_{0}(u)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have <math id="S4.p18.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.p18.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S4.p18.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as its atomic firing sequence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the game proceeds almost identically. However, <math id="S4.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}(u)=c_{0}(u)=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}(u)=c_{0}(u)=n</annotation></semantics></math>. It can be verified that all other vertices have the same number of chips on round <math id="S4.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> as on round 0. Then we again have <math id="S4.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S4.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> as its atomic firing sequence.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 4.7</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 4 Atomic Firing Sequences ‣ Periods and Atomic Firing Sequences of Parallel Chip-Firing Games on Directed Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows an example construction for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1010" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1010</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1010</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n(s)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n(s)=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d(s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d(s)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Chip numbers written beside the vertices in the outermost cycle apply to the corresponding vertices in each cycle. As shown, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(u_{0}^{0})=c_{0}(u_{0}^{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(u_{0}^{0})=c_{0}(u_{0}^{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(u)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(u)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}(v)=s_{0}(2n)+n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}(v)=s_{0}(2n)+n=6</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> fires on rounds 0 and 2, we have <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> fires on round 3. Then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{4}(u_{0}^{0})=c_{4}(u_{0}^{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{4}(u_{0}^{0})=c_{4}(u_{0}^{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
